Fix partition-dependent true DOF counts and wrong P matrix rows for hanging
vertices on partitioned nonconforming meshes.

With an arbitrary (e.g. METIS) partitioning, a hanging vertex interior to a
master edge or face can be owned (minimum rank among elements touching it) by
a rank whose elements touch the refined region only through that vertex. Such
a "fan" rank sees the master and all of its slaves as ghosts, and
ParFiniteElementSpace::BuildParallelConformingInterpolation skips ghost slaves
when building dependencies, so the owner never constrains the vertex and
wrongly counts it as a true DOF with an identity P matrix row. The number of
true DOFs then depends on the partitioning (the symptom of mfem#3925), and the
wrong H1 rows corrupt anything built from the space: in Palace the corrupted
auxiliary-space operators make the multigrid V-cycle amplify instead of
contract, after which left-preconditioned GMRES reports convergence on the
preconditioned residual while the true residual is O(1), and eigensolves
return silently wrong results.

Fix: in ParNCMesh::BuildVertexList, reassign each vertex interior to a master
edge/face to the minimum rank among the owners of the slaves whose closure
contains it. Every rank touching the vertex sees the same master and slave
lists, so the assignment is globally consistent, and the new owner constrains
the vertex through its local slave with the existing dependency code. Fan
ranks receive the finalized row like any other unowned DOF.

Also harden the neighbor-row message decoding (ElementSet::SkipTree and an
invalid-ID skip in NeighborRowMessage::Decode): a receiver that cannot resolve
an encoded refinement subtree now consumes it in sync and ignores the
corresponding rows instead of reading out of bounds.

Applies on top of mfem_ncmesh_tet_edge_face_groups.diff.

